{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. You were brought in because your heart rate was very high at dialysis. Can you tell me about your symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had palpitations off and on for about two weeks. Not really painful, but I feel tired and a bit nauseous. I had chills last night too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your heart rhythm is atrial fibrillation with rapid ventricular response — that means your heart is beating fast and irregularly. We gave you a small dose of metoprolol in the ER to help slow it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this before. It’s hard to control without my blood pressure dropping too low. My cardiologist had planned an ablation in 10 days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, cardiology reviewed your case and decided to move up the ablation. It’s now scheduled sooner. Until then, we’ll manage your rate carefully, especially since you’re on dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I missed my dialysis yesterday because of the high heart rate. Is that going to be a problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be. Your potassium was elevated at 5.9 when you arrived — that’s why we gave you kayexalate. High potassium can affect your heart rhythm. We’ve scheduled dialysis for today to help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know that. So the dialysis will help bring my potassium down and also help my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2158-04-28 01:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Dialysis will help clear excess fluid and electrolytes, which supports your heart. We’ll also continue your home medications, including warfarin for stroke prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2158-04-28 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from this morning show your potassium is now 4.6 — much better. Your blood work didn’t show any signs of infection; both blood cultures were negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2158-04-28 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried the chills meant I was getting sick again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2158-04-28 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The chills could be related to your heart rhythm or fluid shifts. Your chest X-ray shows mild fluid in the lungs, which fits with your history of heart failure, but it’s not severe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2158-04-28 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m about to go to dialysis. Will I be able to go home afterward?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2158-04-28 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, assuming everything goes smoothly with dialysis and your heart rate stays stable. After that, you’ll go home to prepare for your ablation procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2158-04-28 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well on dialysis. Your potassium is now 5.9 again — slightly high, but we expect that post-dialysis fluctuation. More importantly, your heart rate is down to 110 and still irregular, but better controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2158-04-28 13:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my medications? I take metoprolol every other day, but it makes me dizzy sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2158-04-28 13:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve adjusted your dose. You’ll now take 25 mg on dialysis days and 50 mg on non-dialysis days. This should help balance heart rate control and blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re discharging you home. Remember to go to dialysis as scheduled before your ablation. Weigh yourself daily — call if you gain more than 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I continue all my usual meds, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, including warfarin, levothyroxine, and your skin creams for itching. Your TSH was normal, so no changes there. Keep using cetirizine and the topical treatments as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my heart will stay like this — fast — until the ablation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It may stay elevated, but with the medication adjustment and dialysis, we’re keeping it as stable as possible. The ablation should fix the underlying issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I understand. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you soon for the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing — the X-ray mentioned a calcified spot in my abdomen. Should I worry about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s been seen before on prior imaging. It’s not new or concerning — likely an old finding. No action needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, that puts my mind at ease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2158-04-28 18:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Go home, rest, and follow up with your dialysis and cardiology teams. We’ll be monitoring your progress."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2158-04-28 00:49:00",
